{%- comment -%}
  Tells search engines that the Dutch and English pages are the same page in two
  languages.

  The problem this solves:

  /about.html and /en/about.html are two URLs with nearly the same content. Left
  alone, a search engine has to guess whether one is a copy of the other, and it
  may pick the wrong one to show, or show the Dutch page to someone searching in
  English. The hreflang tags below remove the guesswork: they name every language
  version of this page and say which language each one is in. The x-default entry
  says which version to show someone whose language is neither, and points at the
  Dutch page.

  Why this is written by hand:

  Polyglot ships an i18n_headers tag that produces these tags. It cannot be
  used here because it builds each URL from the page's permalink, and ordinary
  pages like about.html do not set one. Only the game files do. Every other page
  would get a broken link.

  Two things here look wrong and are not:

  1. Each href is wrapped in a static_href block. Polyglot rewrites links so that a
     visitor reading English keeps landing on English pages: inside the English
     build, href="/about.html" silently becomes href="/en/about.html". That is
     what you want for a link in the page, and exactly what you do not want here,
     because the whole point of the Dutch entry is to link to the Dutch page.
     static_href marks a link as already correct and stops the rewriting.

  2. The href is written before hreflang, which reads backwards. static_href works
     by writing the attribute out misspelled ("ferh") and spelling it back at the
     end of the build. Polyglot skips that last step for anything directly
     preceded by hreflang="<default language>", so writing the attributes in the
     natural order leaves a misspelled attribute in the HTML and the tag stops
     working. Putting the href first avoids it.

  Pages that only exist in Dutch have nothing to point at, so they get no tags.
  Those are the ones named in exclude_from_localization in _config.yml.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign localised = true -%}
{%- for excluded in site.exclude_from_localization -%}
  {%- if page.path contains excluded -%}{%- assign localised = false -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if localised -%}
  {%- for lang in site.languages %}
    {%- if lang == site.default_lang -%}
      {%- assign alternate_url = page.url -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- assign alternate_url = page.url | prepend: lang | prepend: '/' -%}
    {%- endif %}
    <link rel="alternate" {% static_href %}href="{{ site.url }}{{ alternate_url }}"{% endstatic_href %} hreflang="{{ lang }}" />
  {%- endfor %}
    <link rel="alternate" {% static_href %}href="{{ site.url }}{{ page.url }}"{% endstatic_href %} hreflang="x-default" />
{%- endif -%}
